<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 8.950 percent on Monday from 9.106 percent at the previous auction on May 13.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 991.725 million Egyptian pounds, replace bills worth 874.875 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 900 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 18, 1997 (Nov 11, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.950 percent (9.106).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 991.725 million (991.925 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 2,419.025 million (1,977.850 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.751-8.985 percent (8.814-9.239).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.751-10.200 percent (8.814-10.400).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 90 (178).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 236 (253).</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
